-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA), consolidated version 07-a0-00 (currency start 29 Apr 2026).
-- Part I: the s 3 terms the in-scope provisions use, s 3A, and the nouns every other module reads.
-- Source: sources/rta-1987.07-a0-00.mrdoc_49316.txt (s 3 at lines 15-102, s 3A at 103-106).
-- LQA subject residential-tenancies-act-lqa, step 4A, 4 October 2026. Not yet through 6H.
--
-- Dates are day numbers (days since 1 January 1970) built with the calendar in the jurisdiction
-- library module wa-interpretation-act-1984.l4, of which this folder holds a byte-identical copy.
-- Days and months are counted under Interpretation Act 1984 ss 61 and 62, encoded there.
-- Facts the reference register supplies as inputs (who is a competent court, whether a form is
-- approved, whether a person is a property manager, ...) are fields of the records below; the
-- register entry for each is named in a comment.

IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-1984`

§ `Day numbers and the Interpretation Act 1984 counts, as the in-scope provisions use them`

-- A day number from a year, month and day. Utility; no provision.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day number` y m d MEANS `the day number of` (`the date` y m d)

-- The calendar date of a day number. Utility; no provision.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`the calendar date of day` n MEANS `the date of day number` n

-- s 61(1)(b): "where a period of time is expressed to be reckoned from, or after, a specified day,
-- that day shall not be included in the period". The last day of n days after day d.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the period of` n `days after day` d MEANS
    `the day number of` (`s 61(1)(b) -- the last day of a period of` n `days after` (`the calendar date of day` d))

-- s 61(1)(b) with s 62(2)-(3): a period of n months "after" day d begins on the day after d and
-- ends on the numerically corresponding day, less one, in the nth month after it begins (or the
-- last day of that month). For d = 1 March 2025 and n = 12 the period ends on 1 March 2026.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) ss 61(1)(b), 62(2), 62(3)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the period of` n `months after day` d MEANS
    `the day number of` (`s 62 -- the last day of a period of` n `months beginning on` (`the calendar date of day` (d PLUS 1)))

-- s 62(2)-(3) for a period expressed to begin on day d (s 61(1)(a): d is included).
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) ss 61(1)(a), 62(2), 62(3)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the period of` n `months beginning on day` d MEANS
    `the day number of` (`s 62 -- the last day of a period of` n `months beginning on` (`the calendar date of day` d))

-- s 61(1)(f): "not less than" a number of days between 2 events: both event days are excluded.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(f)
GIVEN first IS A NUMBER, second IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of clear days between day` first `and day` second MEANS
    `s 61(1)(f) -- the number of clear days between` (`the calendar date of day` first) `and` (`the calendar date of day` second)

-- The first day that is "not less than" n days after day d (ss 30(1)(a), 31A(2)(b)(i), 64(2), 64(4)(c)(i)).
-- FK-06, reading taken (A): s 61(1)(f) excludes both event days, so n clear days must lie between d and
-- the day: the first such day is the day after the nth day after d.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b), (f); fork FK-06 reading A
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first day not less than` n `days after day` d MEANS
    `the last day of the period of` n `days after day` d PLUS 1

-- FK-06, reading rejected (B): s 61(1)(b) alone: the nth day after d is itself "not less than n days after" it.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b); fork FK-06 reading B
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`FK-06 reading B -- the first day not less than` n `days after day` d MEANS
    `the last day of the period of` n `days after day` d

-- s 61(1)(g): a number of days between 2 events, not expressed as clear days or "not less than":
-- the first event's day is excluded and the second's included.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(g)
GIVEN first IS A NUMBER, second IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from day` first `to day` second MEANS
    `s 61(1)(g) -- the number of days between` (`the calendar date of day` first) `and` (`the calendar date of day` second)

-- Excluded days (s 61(2)) are supplied as a list of day numbers of the public service, bank and
-- public holidays for the part of the State concerned; Saturdays and Sundays are computed.
GIVEN ns IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Calendar date`
`the calendar dates of days` ns MEANS
    CONSIDER ns
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN n FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (`the calendar date of day` n) FOLLOWED BY (`the calendar dates of days` rest)

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(2)
GIVEN d        IS A NUMBER
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is day` d `an excluded day, given the holidays` holidays IF
    `s 61(2) -- is an excluded day` (`the calendar date of day` d) `given the holidays` (`the calendar dates of days` holidays)

-- s 61(1)(e), (h): where the time for doing a thing expires, or an act is to be done on or before
-- a day, and that day is an excluded day, the thing may be done on the next day that is not.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(e), (h)
GIVEN d        IS A NUMBER
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for a thing due on day` d `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `the day number of` (`s 61(1)(e) -- the last day for doing a thing whose time expires on` (`the calendar date of day` d) `given the holidays` (`the calendar dates of days` holidays))

-- s 61(1)(b), (e): the last day for a thing to be done "within" n days after day d.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN n        IS A NUMBER
      d        IS A NUMBER
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for a thing to be done within` n `days after day` d `, given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    `the last day for a thing due on day` (`the last day of the period of` n `days after day` d) `, given the holidays` holidays

§ `Small utilities (no provision)`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the later of day` a `and day` b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earlier of day` a `and day` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN x  IS A STRING
      xs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
x `is among` xs MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (h EQUALS x) OR (x `is among` rest)

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF STRING
      ys IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some member of` xs `is among` ys MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (h `is among` ys) OR (`some member of` rest `is among` ys)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` m `is` d IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN x EQUALS d

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` m `is before day` d IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN x LESS THAN d

§ `Section 3 -- Terms used, and the facts the in-scope provisions read`

-- s 3 "tenancy period ... whether the agreement is for a fixed term or creates a periodic tenancy".
DECLARE `Kind of tenancy` IS ONE OF
    `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    `a periodic tenancy`

-- ss 27AA(1), 30(1), 31A(1): rent is a fixed amount or is calculated by reference to the tenant's income.
DECLARE `Basis of rent` IS ONE OF
    `a fixed amount`
    `calculated by reference to the tenant's income`

-- The lessor and the tenant, as givers of notices (ss 70A(2), (6), (7)).
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the lessor`
    `the tenant`

-- Status facts that the Regulations, s 29(1)(b)(ii) and s 84 read. Each is supplied as a fact
-- (reference register REF-25, REF-30, REF-36, REF-73, REF-86). A field that a regulation reads
-- names the regulation.
DECLARE `Status facts` HAS
    `the lessor is an employer in the Table to r 5B(2A) and a tenant is its employee`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor is the Housing Authority or a GEHA department and the premises are let to a Government employee under the GEHA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor is the WA Country Health Service and a tenant is employed or engaged by it`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are Butler's Cottage, Government House`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor is an agency in the Table to r 5B(3)`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Crown is the lessor and a tenant is an officer of a department in the Table to r 5B(4)`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Housing Authority is the lessor`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Housing Authority is a party, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the WA Country Health Service is the tenant, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting to its staff` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are a residential unit in Foyer Oxford and the agreement is with Foundation Housing Limited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is the renewal or extension of an agreement`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are south of the 26th parallel of south latitude`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court order under s 84 disapplies s 30(1) or s 31A to the agreement`                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- A notice of termination under s 70A (s 70A(1) "notice").
DECLARE `Notice under s 70A` HAS
    `given by`                 IS A `Party`
    `given on`                 IS A NUMBER
    `possession day specified` IS A NUMBER

-- A residential tenancy agreement (s 3), with the facts the in-scope provisions read about it.
--   `lessor`: the lessor under the agreement at the end of its term; s 3 'lessor' includes a personal
--     representative, successor or assignee of a lessor (fork FK-13 on what that does to s 31B(3)(a)).
--   `granted by`: the lessor who made the agreement (the same person unless the reversion passed).
--   `tenants`: the tenant, or each co-tenant (s 3 'party' para (a)).
--   `premises`: s 3A, the residential premises for which the right to occupy is granted.
--   `entered into on`: the day the agreement was made (ss 99(2)(a), r 5CA(1)(b)).
--   `tenancy commenced on`: the first day of the tenancy under it (ss 29(3), 30(1)(b), 31A(2)(b)(ii),
--     31B(2)(c) "starts").
--   `expiry day`: s 3, for a fixed term only.
--   `weekly rent`: the rent the agreement itself sets when its tenancy commences.
--   `the amount or method of an increase is set out`: s 30(2)(a).
--   `provides that the rent may increase`: s 30(2)(a) as modified by r 5CA.
--   `rent increases excluded by agreement`: s 30(2)(b) (a limit short of exclusion is a field of the notice).
--   `notices under s 70A`: every notice under s 70A given in relation to the agreement.
--   `possession delivered up on`: the day the tenant delivered up possession, if the tenant has.
--   `terminated on`: the day the agreement terminated under s 60, if it has (an input decided by
--     the s 60 rule in part-5-termination.l4 or supplied as a fact, REF-53 to REF-63).
DECLARE `Residential tenancy agreement` HAS
    `name`                                           IS A STRING
    `lessor`                                         IS A STRING
    `granted by`                                     IS A STRING
    `tenants`                                        IS A LIST OF STRING
    `premises`                                       IS A STRING
    `kind`                                           IS A `Kind of tenancy`
    `rent basis`                                     IS A `Basis of rent`
    `entered into on`                                IS A NUMBER
    `tenancy commenced on`                           IS A NUMBER
    `expiry day`                                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `weekly rent`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides that the rent may increase`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `notices under s 70A`                            IS A LIST OF `Notice under s 70A`
    `possession delivered up on`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `terminated on`                                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `status`                                         IS A `Status facts`

-- The provision under which rent was varied. The two versions of ss 30 and 31A are those before
-- and from 29 July 2024, when the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2024 ss 25-26 came into
-- operation (SL 2024/143 cl. 2(f); reference register REF-41).
DECLARE `Provision` IS ONE OF
    `section 30`
    `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024`
    `section 31A`
    `section 31A as in force before 29 July 2024`

-- An increase of rent (s 30) or a change of the method of calculating rent (s 31A) that has taken
-- effect: the history ss 30(1)(b), 31A(2)(b)(ii) and 31B read.
DECLARE `Rent variation` HAS
    `agreement`             IS A STRING
    `under`                 IS A `Provision`
    `notice given on`       IS A NUMBER
    `took effect on`        IS A NUMBER
    `weekly rent from then` IS A NUMBER

-- Every agreement for the premises (in any order) and every variation that has taken effect.
DECLARE `Rent history` HAS
    `agreements` IS A LIST OF `Residential tenancy agreement`
    `variations` IS A LIST OF `Rent variation`

-- How a notice is given (s 85; regulations 7FA, 12I).
DECLARE `Way of giving a notice` IS ONE OF
    `personally (s 85(1)(a))`
    `by post (s 85(1)(b))`
    `by email (s 85(1)(c))`
    `left at the premises by the Housing Authority (r 7FA)`
    `to a person apparently over 16 apparently residing at the premises (s 85(4)(a))`
    `to the person who ordinarily pays the rent (s 85(4)(b))`

-- r 12I(1) "authorised notice" (notices under ss 11F(2), 11G(1), 11J(1), 11L(2), 81F(2), 81Q(1)
-- and r 15(2)); every notice under an in-scope provision is of the second kind.
DECLARE `Kind of notice` IS ONE OF
    `an authorised notice (r 12I(1))`
    `a notice under an in-scope provision (ss 30, 31A, 31, 64, 70A)`

DECLARE `Giving of a notice` HAS
    `way`                                                         IS A `Way of giving a notice`
    `kind of notice`                                              IS A `Kind of notice`
    `on`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`    IS A NUMBER
    `the recipient consented to electronic service`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient's email was given to the bond administrator with a bond record or release application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Housing Authority is the lessor and gives it`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- The form of a notice (ss 30(1), 31A(2) "the approved form"; before 29 July 2024 "a form
-- approved by the Minister"). Whether a form is approved is a fact (REF-01).
DECLARE `Form of a notice` IS ONE OF
    `the approved form (s 88C)`
    `a form approved by the Minister`
    `no approved form`

-- A notice of increase of rent under s 30, or of a change of method under s 31A (which ss 31(1A)
-- and 100(4) also call a notice of increase of rent).
--   `given by the lessor`: by the lessor or a property manager as its agent (s 86B, REF-87).
--   `within any limit agreed under s 30(2)(b)`: the increase is within any limit the parties agreed.
--   `any departure from the required form is immaterial and not misleading`: Interpretation Act s 74,
--     read by fork FK-26 when a notice is in one approved form and the section requires the other.
DECLARE `Notice of increase of rent` HAS
    `under`                                      IS A `Provision`
    `agreement`                                  IS A STRING
    `given by the lessor`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `form`                                       IS A `Form of a notice`
    `specifies the increased rent or the change` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the day`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `given`                                      IS A `Giving of a notice`
    `takes effect on`                            IS A NUMBER
    `weekly rent from then`                      IS A NUMBER
    `withdrawn`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `within any limit agreed under s 30(2)(b)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `any departure from the required form is immaterial and not misleading` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3 "expiry day"
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 3 -- the expiry day of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `kind`
    WHEN `a tenancy for a fixed term` THEN a's `expiry day`
    WHEN `a periodic tenancy` THEN NOTHING

-- s 3 "party", para (a): the lessor, and the tenant or each co-tenant.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3 "party" para (a)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 3 -- the parties to` a MEANS (a's `lessor`) FOLLOWED BY (a's `tenants`)

-- s 3 "residential tenancy agreement": an agreement, written or not, express or implied, under
-- which a person for valuable consideration grants another a right to occupy residential premises
-- for the purpose of residence. Whether the Act then applies (s 5) is a fact (REF-84).
DECLARE `Arrangement to occupy` HAS
    `for valuable consideration`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `grants a right to occupy, exclusively or otherwise`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises constitute or are intended to constitute a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for the purpose of residence`                                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3 "residential tenancy agreement", "residential premises"
GIVEN x IS AN `Arrangement to occupy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the arrangement is a residential tenancy agreement` x IF
        "for valuable consideration" ... x's `for valuable consideration`
    AND "grants ... a right to occupy" ... x's `grants a right to occupy, exclusively or otherwise`
    AND "residential premises" ... x's `the premises constitute or are intended to constitute a place of residence`
    AND "for the purpose of residence" ... x's `for the purpose of residence`

-- s 3 "rent": "a payment under a residential tenancy agreement payable by the tenant in respect of
-- the tenancy period or part of the tenancy period".
DECLARE `Payment` HAS
    `under the agreement and payable by the tenant`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `in respect of the tenancy period or part of it`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `as security for the performance of the tenant's obligations`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `an amount for pet damage or fumigation under s 29(1)(b)(ii)`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3 "rent"
GIVEN p IS A `Payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the payment is rent` p IF
        p's `under the agreement and payable by the tenant`
    AND p's `in respect of the tenancy period or part of it`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3 "security bond"
GIVEN p IS A `Payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the payment is a security bond` p IF
        "an amount paid or payable by a tenant as security for the performance of the tenant's obligations"
    ..  p's `as security for the performance of the tenant's obligations`
    OR  "including an amount referred to in section 29(1)(b)(ii)" ... p's `an amount for pet damage or fumigation under s 29(1)(b)(ii)`

-- s 3 "pet means an animal other than an assistance animal". Whether an animal is an assistance
-- animal (Dog Act 1976 s 8(1), accreditation, training) is a fact (REF-06).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3 "pet", "assistance animal"
GIVEN `the animal is an assistance animal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- the animal is a pet, given whether it is an assistance animal:` `the animal is an assistance animal` IF
    NOT `the animal is an assistance animal`

-- s 3 "tenancy period": the whole period during which the agreement is in force, whether it is for
-- a fixed term or creates a periodic tenancy. Day d falls in it if d is on or after the day the
-- tenancy commenced and the agreement has not terminated before d.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3 "tenancy period", "tenancy"
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- day` d `falls in the tenancy period of` a IF
        d AT LEAST a's `tenancy commenced on`
    AND (CONSIDER a's `terminated on`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST t THEN d AT MOST t)

§ `Section 3A -- References to residential premises or premises`

-- s 3A(1)-(2): in a provision relating to an agreement (including one that refers to its lessor or
-- tenant), "the premises" are the residential premises for which the agreement grants a right to occupy.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 3A(1), (2)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 3A -- the premises of` a MEANS a's `premises`

§ `Constructors for the cases (no provision)`

`no special status` MEANS `Status facts` WITH
    `the lessor is an employer in the Table to r 5B(2A) and a tenant is its employee`                       IS FALSE
    `the lessor is the Housing Authority or a GEHA department and the premises are let to a Government employee under the GEHA` IS FALSE
    `the lessor is the WA Country Health Service and a tenant is employed or engaged by it`                IS FALSE
    `the premises are Butler's Cottage, Government House`                                                  IS FALSE
    `the lessor is an agency in the Table to r 5B(3)`                                                      IS FALSE
    `the Crown is the lessor and a tenant is an officer of a department in the Table to r 5B(4)`           IS FALSE
    `the Housing Authority is the lessor`                                                                  IS FALSE
    `the Housing Authority is a party, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting` IS FALSE
    `the WA Country Health Service is the tenant, and the agreement provides for and was entered into for sub-letting to its staff` IS FALSE
    `the premises are a residential unit in Foyer Oxford and the agreement is with Foundation Housing Limited` IS FALSE
    `the agreement is the renewal or extension of an agreement`                                            IS FALSE
    `the premises are south of the 26th parallel of south latitude`                                        IS TRUE
    `the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises`                                                IS FALSE
    `a court order under s 84 disapplies s 30(1) or s 31A to the agreement`                                IS FALSE

-- `no special status` takes the premises to be south of the 26th parallel, as Perth is (r 10AD).

-- A fixed-term agreement with no s 70A notice, not terminated, whose rent is a fixed amount and
-- whose increases are not set out.
GIVEN n      IS A STRING
      l      IS A STRING
      ts     IS A LIST OF STRING
      p      IS A STRING
      start  IS A NUMBER
      expiry IS A NUMBER
      rent   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`a fixed term` n `between` l `and` ts `for` p `from day` start `to day` expiry `at weekly rent` rent MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS n
        `lessor`                                         IS l
        `granted by`                                     IS l
        `tenants`                                        IS ts
        `premises`                                       IS p
        `kind`                                           IS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
        `rent basis`                                     IS `a fixed amount`
        `entered into on`                                IS start
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS start
        `expiry day`                                     IS JUST expiry
        `weekly rent`                                    IS rent
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS FALSE
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS EMPTY
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS NOTHING
        `terminated on`                                  IS NOTHING
        `status`                                         IS `no special status`

-- A periodic agreement, not terminated, whose rent is a fixed amount.
GIVEN n      IS A STRING
      l      IS A STRING
      ts     IS A LIST OF STRING
      p      IS A STRING
      start  IS A NUMBER
      rent   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Residential tenancy agreement`
`the periodic agreement` n `between` l `and` ts `for` p `from day` start `at weekly rent` rent MEANS
    `Residential tenancy agreement` WITH
        `name`                                           IS n
        `lessor`                                         IS l
        `granted by`                                     IS l
        `tenants`                                        IS ts
        `premises`                                       IS p
        `kind`                                           IS `a periodic tenancy`
        `rent basis`                                     IS `a fixed amount`
        `entered into on`                                IS start
        `tenancy commenced on`                           IS start
        `expiry day`                                     IS NOTHING
        `weekly rent`                                    IS rent
        `the amount or method of an increase is set out` IS FALSE
        `provides that the rent may increase`            IS FALSE
        `rent increases excluded by agreement`           IS FALSE
        `notices under s 70A`                            IS EMPTY
        `possession delivered up on`                     IS NOTHING
        `terminated on`                                  IS NOTHING
        `status`                                         IS `no special status`

-- A notice handed to the recipient personally on day d.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Giving of a notice`
`handed over on day` d MEANS
    `Giving of a notice` WITH
        `way`                                                      IS `personally (s 85(1)(a))`
        `kind of notice`                                           IS `a notice under an in-scope provision (ss 30, 31A, 31, 64, 70A)`
        `on`                                                       IS d
        `day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS d
        `the recipient consented to electronic service`            IS FALSE
        `the recipient's email was given to the bond administrator with a bond record or release application` IS FALSE
        `the Housing Authority is the lessor and gives it`         IS FALSE

-- A notice of increase of rent under the current s 30, complete in form, handed over on day g,
-- for an increase to weekly rent r from day e.
GIVEN ag IS A STRING, g IS A NUMBER, r IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Notice of increase of rent`
`a s 30 notice under` ag `given on day` g `for weekly rent` r `from day` e MEANS
    `Notice of increase of rent` WITH
        `under`                                      IS `section 30`
        `agreement`                                  IS ag
        `given by the lessor`                        IS TRUE
        `in writing`                                 IS TRUE
        `form`                                       IS `the approved form (s 88C)`
        `specifies the increased rent or the change` IS TRUE
        `specifies the day`                          IS TRUE
        `given`                                      IS `handed over on day` g
        `takes effect on`                            IS e
        `weekly rent from then`                      IS r
        `withdrawn`                                  IS FALSE
        `within any limit agreed under s 30(2)(b)`   IS TRUE
        `any departure from the required form is immaterial and not misleading` IS TRUE
